@participant22 are you aware of this issue? Look at the video above from October 8. My app is appearing exactly the same: when started up, the splash screen immediately disappears, and a black or gray background is shown. After a short amount of time, my app hides the splash screen and my home screen appears. This makes `expo-splash-screen` completely unusable.

@participant22 here are some detailed steps to reproduce this:

1. Create a `create-expo-app@latest`. I ran this just now, version was `create-expo-app@3.2.0`.
2. In `app/_layout.tsx`, change the `useEffect` code to the following to simulate a longer loading time:

```
  useEffect(() => {
    if (loaded) {
      setTimeout(() => {
        SplashScreen.hideAsync();
      }, 1000);
    }
  }, [loaded]);
```

3. Run it in the simulator a few times. Sometimes the splash screen will work fine, but sometimes not:

https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/664a7820-0991-4c2f-8490-254de2349d9c

The full code that was used for this screen recording can be found here:

https://github.com/participant21/expo-31875-repro

